  "worked_solution": "Since we are given that the face diagonal of the cube is $10\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}$, its side length $s$ is $10\\,\\text{cm}.$ Now, the volume of a cube with side length $s$ is given by \n\n$$\nV=V(s)={s}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{s}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=10$ gives\n\n$$\n{V}^{\u2032}(10)=3(10)^{2}=300.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the container is increasing when the face diagonal is $10\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}$ is $300\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}.$",
